Signing nothing, so taken without a key (trust=unsigned in fixes/UPSTREAMS, the
owner's choice, 2026-11-22): their commits are used from their official git as
it stands, a release tag or a branch head, with no signature checked.
postgresql-18    git.postgresql.org: its tags are unsigned and it publishes no
                 tarball signatures.
glibc            sourceware.org: it makes no point releases, so its fixes are on
                 release branches, which no one signs.
